 !!! Note
     The minimum last stake amount can be configured using `last_stake_amount_min_ratio` - which defaults to 0.5 (50%). This means that the minimum stake amount that's ever used is `stake_amount * 0.5`. This avoids very low stake amounts, that are close to the minimum tradable amount for the pair and can be refused by the exchange.
 
+#### Limiting exposure to a single underlying currency
+
+If several of your pairs are priced against, or settled in, the same underlying currency (for example multiple pairs quoted in the same stablecoin, or several futures contracts margined in the same currency), a large adverse move in that currency can hit all of those positions at once - even though each trade looked fine in isolation.
+
+`max_currency_exposure` limits how much of your tradable capital may be committed, across all currently open trades, to positions sharing the same underlying (quote/settlement) currency. It's expressed as a ratio of the [tradable balance](#tradable-balance), e.g. `max_currency_exposure=0.5` allows at most 50% of the tradable capital to be tied up in trades sharing one underlying currency at the same time.
+
+When opening (or increasing) a trade would push the combined exposure to that currency above the configured limit, the stake amount for that trade is reduced to fit under the limit. If no stake would remain, the trade is not opened (respectively, not increased). This is logged the same way as other stake-sizing adjustments.
+
+This setting is disabled (no cap applied) unless explicitly configured, and can be set per-strategy [like other strategy parameters](#parameters-in-the-strategy).
+
+!!! Note
+    Since freqtrade pairs are all quoted in the same configured `stake_currency`, this setting most commonly caps the total capital committed to all open trades at once - complementing `tradable_balance_ratio` with a hard, per-strategy ceiling on live exposure.
+
 #### Static stake amount
 
 The `stake_amount` configuration statically configures the amount of stake-currency your bot will use for each trade.
